---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const lastUpdated = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);
---

<Layout
    title="Terms of Service | BatteryTrail"
    description="The terms and conditions governing your use of BatteryTrail, including content disclaimers and affiliate disclosures."
>
    <Header />

    <main class="flex-grow w-full max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
        <div class="mb-10 border-b border-[#224249] pb-8">
            <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-white leading-[1.15]">
                Terms of Service
            </h1>
            <p class="mt-4 text-sm font-medium text-text-muted">
                Last updated: {lastUpdated}
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="prose prose-lg dark:prose-invert max-w-none prose-a:text-primary prose-a:no-underline hover:prose-a:underline">
            <p>
                These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your access to and use of
                the BatteryTrail website (the "Site"). By accessing or using the
                Site, you agree to be bound by these Terms. If you do not agree,
                please do not use the Site.
            </p>

            <h2>About the Site</h2>
            <p>
                BatteryTrail publishes educational and editorial content about
                batteries and mobile power systems, including RV batteries, ebike
                batteries, lithium battery technology, and off-grid power. Our
                content is intended for general informational purposes only.
            </p>

            <h2>Editorial Standards</h2>
            <p>
                We strive to provide accurate, useful, and current information. We
                research and compare products, and we may update or correct content
                over time. However, product specifications, prices, availability,
                and warranties change frequently and are controlled by
                manufacturers and retailers, not by BatteryTrail.
            </p>

            <h2>No Warranty and Disclaimer of Liability</h2>
            <p>
                THE SITE AND ALL CONTENT ARE PROVIDED ON AN "AS IS" AND "AS
                AVAILABLE" BASIS WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND, EITHER EXPRESS OR
                IMPLIED. To the fullest extent permitted by law, BatteryTrail
                disclaims all warranties and will not be liable for any damages
                arising from your use of, or reliance on, the Site or its content.
            </p>
            <p>
                Battery work can be hazardous. Always follow the manufacturer's
                instructions and applicable safety codes, and consult a qualified
                professional for your specific installation. Nothing on this Site
                constitutes professional electrical, engineering, or safety advice.
            </p>

            <h2>Affiliate Disclosure</h2>
            <p>
                Some links on the Site are affiliate links. If you click an
                affiliate link and make a purchase, we may earn a commission at no
                additional cost to you. This helps support the Site and our work.
                We aim to recommend products based on genuine evaluation, and
                affiliate relationships do not change the price you pay. For more
                information, see our
                <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
            </p>

            <h2>Intellectual Property</h2>
            <p>
                All content on the Site, including text, graphics, logos, and
                images, is the property of BatteryTrail or its content suppliers
                and is protected by applicable copyright and trademark laws. You
                may view and share our content for personal, non-commercial use
                with attribution, but you may not reproduce or republish it
                commercially without our prior written consent.
            </p>

            <h2>Acceptable Use</h2>
            <p>
                You agree not to use the Site in any way that is unlawful, harmful,
                or that interferes with the Site's operation or other users'
                enjoyment of it. You may not attempt to gain unauthorized access to
                the Site or its systems.
            </p>

            <h2>Third-Party Links</h2>
            <p>
                The Site contains links to third-party websites, products, and
                services. We are not responsible for the content, accuracy, or
                practices of those third parties. Your dealings with them are
                solely between you and the third party.
            </p>

            <h2>Changes to These Terms</h2>
            <p>
                We may revise these Terms at any time. The "Last updated" date at
                the top of this page reflects the most recent revision. Continued
                use of the Site after changes are posted constitutes acceptance of
                the revised Terms.
            </p>

            <h2>Governing Law</h2>
            <p>
                These Terms are governed by the laws of the jurisdiction in which
                BatteryTrail operates, without regard to conflict-of-law
                principles.
            </p>

            <h2>Contact</h2>
            <p>
                Questions about these Terms? Contact us at
                <a href="mailto:chesterbeard@salishseaconsulting.com">chesterbeard@salishseaconsulting.com</a>.
            </p>
        </div>
    </main>

    <Footer />
</Layout>
